    description: "Add a session-end / cooldown step to `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/recover-state-playbook.md` that prompts the agent to refresh `agent_notes.json` with cross-session signal before signing off.\n\n**Motivating incident (session_retrospective_04262026_1911.md Finding 7 / 1736.md Finding 3):** During the 2026-04-25→26 session, the stop hook never fired (199 user interjections kept the agent in an active turn for ~13.5 hours), so hook-owned state files drifted: `last_completed_utc` stayed at the *prior* session's timestamp, `bakeoff_session_path` continued to point at a 17-day-old workdir even after the agent had created and run a fresh deep bakeoff, and `agent_notes.json` was not updated by the agent during the session. By session end, the agent had filed WI-nutin (P1) and discovered the INV-rahib regression — both of which are exactly the kind of cross-session signal `agent_notes.json` exists to carry. Neither was captured. The next session re-discovered both via `tracker show` rather than via the notes file.\n\n**The notes file vs. the hook state file:** per `recover-state-playbook.md`, two files in `~/<repo>_lab_notebook/guidance_log/` carry post-compaction recovery state:\n- `stop_hook_state.json` — hook-owned (lazy, written only on Stop): `last_completed_utc`, `current_branch`, `guidance_file`, `bakeoff_session_path`, etc.\n- `agent_notes.json` — agent-owned (free-text, written via `scripts/agent-notes --set/--append`): `notes` field for things-the-next-session-needs-to-know.\n\nThe recover-state playbook describes *reading* `agent_notes.json` at session start but does not prescribe *writing* it at session end. That asymmetry is the bug.\n\n**Proposed addition to recover-state-playbook.md:**\n\n```\n### Session-end agent-notes refresh (write side of the recovery loop)\n\nBefore signing off — i.e., when you have completed all in-flight work, no\ntodos remain, and no auto-pr is pending — append a one-paragraph summary\nto `agent_notes.json` capturing what the next session needs to know:\n\n    scripts/agent-notes --append \"<one or two sentences>\"\n\nWhat to include (in priority order):\n1. **Open invariant violations or P1+ defects you discovered.** Reference\n   the tracker ID. Example: \"WI-nutin filed P1 — TRACKER_SYNC_PENDING\n   marker leaks on SIGKILL; needs flock(2) refactor.\"\n2. **Status changes on previously-tracked invariants.** Example: \"INV-rahib\n   re-opened from satisfied -> needs_human_review after PR #3392/#3393\n   regression.\"\n3. **Cross-cutting context the tracker doesn't capture cleanly.** Example:\n   \"Bakeoff workdir is now deep-20260425-210357; prior pointer in\n   stop_hook_state.json was stale by 17 days.\"\n4. **Any ad-hoc shell state the next session would otherwise re-derive.**\n   Example: \"TRACKER_SYNC_PENDING removed manually at 05:52; root cause\n   filed as WI-nutin.\"\n\nKeep it under ~5 lines. The notes file is a working hand-off, not a log;\nverbose entries dilute signal. The retro file (lab notebook) is where\ndetailed analysis goes.\n```\n\n**Optional follow-up (governance, separate item):** a stop hook nudge that fires when `agent_notes.json` mtime is older than the current session's start time. Surfaces in stop guidance: \"agent_notes.json is stale; consider `scripts/agent-notes --append <one-liner>` before stopping.\" This part touches `.agent/hooks/` and is governance — file as a child item *if* the playbook-only change proves insufficient.\n\n**Why this is mostly non-governance:** `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/recover-state-playbook.md` is not in the AGENTS.md governance allowlist. The playbook edit can land via standard auto-pr without the human-review gate. Only the optional stop-hook nudge would need human review, and only if it's actually built.\n\n**Implementation steps:**\n1. Edit `recover-state-playbook.md` with the new section.\n2. Update the playbook's hook summary in `.agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py:PLAYBOOKS` to mention the write-side step (this hook file IS governance — separate review on this step alone, or batch it under the AGENTS.md governance approval umbrella along with the companion items).\n3. Defer the stop-hook nudge to a child item; gather evidence first that the playbook addition alone isn't sufficient.\n\n**Tests:** documentation change; covered by the hook-summary unit test asserting the summary contains the write-side phrase.\n\n**Cross-references:**\n- session_retrospective_04262026_1911.md Finding 7 (write-side gap).\n- session_retrospective_04262026_1736.md Finding 3 (stop hook silence in long human-steered runs — the underlying mechanical reason the write side doesn't happen automatically).\n- `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/recover-state-playbook.md` (file being edited).\n- `scripts/agent-notes` (the existing CLI the playbook will tell agents to use)."  # a884
    fields: {}  # a884
